4A)(h) inserted by S.I. 2026/1063 reg. 4(5) reg. 49(4A)(i) inserted by S.I. 2026/1072 reg. 3(5) reg. 74(9)(bg) inserted by S.I. 2026/1063 reg. 4(6) reg. 74(9)(bh) inserted by S.I. 2026/1072 reg. 3(6) Changes and effects yet to be applied to the whole Instrument associated Parts and Chapters: Whole provisions yet to be inserted into this Instrument (including any effects on those provisions): Sch. 5 para. 35(1A)(g) inserted by S.I. 2026/1063 reg. 4(7)(a) Sch. 5 para. 35(1A)(h) inserted by S.I. 2026/1072 reg. 3(7)(a) reg. 42(7A)(g) inserted by S.I. 2026/1063 reg. 4(3) reg. 42(7A)(h) inserted by S.I. 2026/1072 reg. 3(3) reg. 49(4A)(h) inserted by S.I. 2026/1063 reg. 4(5) reg. 49(4A)(i) inserted by S.I. 2026/1072 reg. 3(5) reg. 74(9)(bg) inserted by S.I. 2026/1063 reg. 4(6) reg. 74(9)(bh) inserted by S.I. 2026/1072 reg. 3(6) Cases in which section 1(1A) of the Administration Act is disapplied E+W+S This section has no associated Explanatory Memorandum 4. Section 1(1A) of the Administration Act (requirement to state national insurance number) shall not apply—&#xD; (a) to a claim for housing benefit where the person making the claim, or in respect of whom the claim is made, is liable to make payments in respect of a dwelling which is a hostel; &#xD; (b) to any child or young person in respect of whom housing benefit is claimed. &#xD; [ F1 (c) to a person who— &#xD; (i) is a person in respect of whom a claim for housing benefit is made; &#xD; (ii) is subject to immigration control within the meaning of section 115(9)(a) of the Immigration and Asylum Act; &#xD; (iii) is a person from abroad for the purposes of these Regulations as defined in regulation 10(2); and &#xD; (iv) has not previously been allocated a national insurance number. ] &#xD; Textual Amendments F1 Reg. 4(c) added (6.4.2009) by The Social Security (National Insurance Number Information: Exemption) Regulations 2009 (S.I. 2009/471) , regs. 1 , 9 Previous: Provision Next: Provision Back to top Options/Help Pri